# Targets removed from the home directory on every `chezmoi apply`.
#
# chezmoi only looks at the current state of the source directory -- it has no
# history, so deleting a `dot_*` file here does NOT delete the file it already
# deployed to existing machines. Listing the target here does.
#
# Entries are permanent while they are listed: anything matching is deleted on
# every apply, so only list paths that must never exist on a managed machine.
# The package half of the same problem lives in the
# `run_onchange_after_*-remove-dependencies.*` scripts.
# See `.docs/dependency-lifecycle.md`.

# `keychain` state directory -- removed in bec4050 (2026-07-23), orphaned when
# Android switched to a fixed agent socket (`~/.ssh/agent.sock`) managed
# directly by `dot_zshrc.tmpl`. The stale `<host>-sh` files here only advertise
# dead random-path sockets.
.keychain

# Cursor -- removed in 601cbeb (2026-07-21), previously managed as dot_cursor/
.cursor

# Gemini CLI -- removed in 601cbeb (2026-07-21)
.gemini

# `claude-omni` and `claude-omni-task` -- removed in #260 (2026-10-27). Its profile,
# ~/.claude-omni, is a one-time `path:` tombstone in the Linux removal script.
.local/bin/claude-omni
.local/bin/claude-omni-task

# `claude-local` and `claude-remote` -- removed in #233 (2026-10-15), replaced by
# `claude-omni` (itself removed in #260). `claude-local-task` became `claude-omni-task`
# in the same change.
.local/bin/claude-local
.local/bin/claude-remote
.local/bin/claude-local-task

# The OmniRoute Compose file -- deployed to ~/local-services by mistake until #233
# (2026-10-15), which ignores `local-services`: the stack runs from the dotfiles checkout,
# where its `.env` lives, and this copy only drifted from it.
local-services/omniroute/compose.yaml

# The folder watcher itself -- removed in PR #276 (2026-10-27). chezmoi no longer ships
# `dot_scripts/executable_linux-toolbox-watch-compress-folders.sh`, so the deployed copy is
# orphaned in `$HOME`; `run_onchange_after_linux-001-stop-folder-watcher.sh` stops any
# instance still running, which would otherwise re-add the removed files to the source.
.scripts/linux-toolbox-watch-compress-folders.sh

# The kube-contexts archive -- orphaned in PR #276 (2026-10-27), which retired the folder
# watcher and stopped syncing `~/.kube`. The old `encrypted_config-files.tar.age` deployed
# this tarball beside the extracted `~/.kube/config-files/`; the folder is what the shell
# actually reads, so the stale archive is removed. The folder itself is left in place.
.kube/config-files.tar

# The `op-retry.cmd` shim -- added by #281 and removed by #282 (2026-10-29). Run through it, every
# op call had a new cmd.exe as its parent, and 1Password for Windows ties an approval to the
# process that runs op, so each item asked for an approval of its own; chezmoi runs `op.exe`
# itself again. It only ever existed on Windows.
.local/bin/op-retry.cmd
